+  "title": "Positivity of Saito's Eta Products",
+  "statement": "For every natural number $h$, does the eta product $\\eta(h\\tau)^{\\varphi(h)}\\prod_{d\\mid h}\\eta(d\\tau)^{-\\mu(d)}$ have only nonnegative Fourier coefficients? In particular, prove or disprove this conjecture when $h$ is divisible by at least two distinct primes.",
+  "background": "Collected from Oberwolfach Reports, which document mathematical workshops and their open-problem discussions.\n\n**Source report:** [Gitter und Anwendungen (2005), Oberwolfach Reports, DOI 10.4171/owr/2005/01, pp. 5--67](https://doi.org/10.4171/owr/2005/01)\n\n## Literature review (checked 2026-08-21)\n\n**Status:** open\n\n**Assessment.** The sentence only says that one unnamed conjecture contains another in special cases; the conjectures themselves are absent from the extracted record.\n\n**Sources checked.**\n\n- [original OWR report](https://doi.org/10.4171/owr/2005/01)\n\nThis is a dated literature triage derived from the supplied OWR curation; verify time-sensitive status and cited claims independently.",
